$\begin{align}
\left(10^1\right)^{3}&=10^{1\cdot 3}
\\\\
&=10^{3}
\end{align}$

This follows from the general rule $\left(x^m\right)^{n}=x^{m\cdot n}$.

We can also see this is correct by expanding the powers.

$\begin{align}
\left(10^1\right)^{3}&=\underbrace{10^1\cdot 10^1\cdot 10^1}_\text{3 times}
\\\\\\
&=\underbrace{
\underbrace{10}_\text{1 time}
\cdot \underbrace{10}_\text{1 time}
\cdot \underbrace{10}_\text{1 time}}
_\text{3 times}
\\\\
&=10^{3}
\end{align}$
